.Dd October 20, 2026
.Dt VIS 1
.Os PUtils
.Sh NAME
.Nm vis ,
.Nm visual
.Nd visual SSH terminal with desktop-like experience
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl r
.Op Fl c Ar config
.Nm visual
.Op Ar same options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
and
.Nm visual
are the same command.
.Nm
connects to a remote SSH server and presents a full-screen terminal
interface that resembles a desktop environment.
It supports split panes, a file manager for drag-and-drop-like file
transfers, multiple tabs, and seamless SFTP integration.

When invoked without arguments,
.Nm
reads its configuration from
.Pa ~/.config/vis/config
and connects to the default host specified there.
When invoked with piped input, it treats the input as a full SSH command
and connects accordingly.

.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl s
Stop any running
.Nm
process and convert the session to a standard SSH workflow.
This sends a cleanup signal to the running instance and exits.
.It Fl h
Clean
.Nm Ns 's
own commands from the shell history before exiting.
.It Fl r
Read-only mode.
Disables all write operations including file uploads, command execution
that modifies state, and configuration changes.
.It Fl c Ar config
Use an alternate configuration file instead of the default.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Nm
looks for its configuration file at
.Pa ~/.config/vis/config .
If it does not exist, a default configuration is created on first run.
The configuration file uses a simple
.Ar key Ns = Ns Ar value
format.

.Pp
Key configuration sections:

.Ss SSH Connection
.Bl -tag -width "identity_file"
.It default_host
The default SSH host to connect to (e.g., "user@host").
.It default_port
SSH port (default: 22).
.It auth_method
Authentication method: "key", "password", or "agent".
.It identity_file
Path to SSH private key (default: ~/.ssh/id_ed25519).
.It timeout
Connection timeout in seconds (default: 30).
.It keepalive_interval
SSH keepalive interval in seconds (default: 60).
.El

.Ss Terminal
.Bl -tag -width "scrollback_lines"
.It term_type
Terminal type to request (default: "xterm-256color").
.It term_cols, term_rows
Default terminal dimensions (default: 120x40).
.It scrollback_lines
Scrollback buffer size (default: 10000).
.It theme
Color theme name (default: "default").
.It show_status_bar, show_tab_bar
Show status and tab bars (default: true).
.El

.Ss Desktop Features
.Bl -tag -width "file_manager_position"
.It enable_file_manager
Enable the file manager pane (default: true).
.It file_manager_width
Width of file manager in columns (default: 30).
.It file_manager_position
Position: "left" or "right" (default: "left").
.It auto_refresh_file_manager
Auto-refresh directory listing (default: true).
.It refresh_interval
Refresh interval in seconds (default: 5).
.It enable_sftp
Enable SFTP file transfers (default: true).
.It local_download_dir
Local directory for downloads (default: ~/Downloads/vis).
.It remote_upload_dir
Remote directory for uploads (default: ~).
.It max_transfer_size
Maximum file transfer size in bytes (default: 100MB).
.El

.Ss Behavior
.Bl -tag -width "reconnect_attempts"
.It read_only_mode
Start in read-only mode (default: false).
.It clean_history_on_exit
Clean shell history on exit (default: false).
.It confirm_close
Prompt before closing (default: true).
.It reconnect_on_disconnect
Auto-reconnect on disconnect (default: false).
.It reconnect_attempts
Number of reconnect attempts (default: 3).
.It reconnect_delay
Delay between reconnects in seconds (default: 5).
.It log_level
Log level: "debug", "info", "warn", "error" (default: "info").
.It log_file
Log file path (default: ~/.local/share/vis/vis.log).
.El

.Ss Key Bindings
All key bindings are configurable.
Defaults use vim-style bindings:
.Bl -tag -width "key_toggle_file_manager"
.It key_quit
Quit (default: Ctrl+q).
.It key_new_tab
New tab (default: Ctrl+t).
.It key_close_tab
Close tab (default: Ctrl+w).
.It key_next_tab
Next tab (default: Ctrl+Tab).
.It key_prev_tab
Previous tab (default: Ctrl+Shift+Tab).
.It key_split_horizontal
Split pane horizontally (default: Ctrl+h).
.It key_split_vertical
Split pane vertically (default: Ctrl+v).
.It key_toggle_file_manager
Toggle file manager (default: Ctrl+f).
.It key_command_mode
Enter command mode (default: :).
.It key_search
Enter search mode (default: /).
.El
.Sh USAGE
.Ss Interactive Mode
Run
.Nm
without arguments to start an interactive session with the configured
default host.
The interface provides:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Multiple tabs (Ctrl+t, Ctrl+w)
.It
Split panes (Ctrl+h, Ctrl+v)
.It
File manager pane (Ctrl+f) for browsing and transferring files
.It
Command mode (:) for internal commands
.It
Search mode (/) for searching scrollback
.El

.Ss Piped Mode
Pipe an SSH command to
.Nm
to connect using that command:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ echo user@example.com | vis
.Ed
This is useful for one-off connections or when the command is generated
by a script.

.Ss File Transfers
In the file manager (Ctrl+f):
.Bl -bullet
.It
Navigate with arrow keys, Enter to enter directories
.It
Space to select files
.It
d to download selected files to local machine
.It
u to upload files from local machine
.It
n to create new directory
.It
r to rename selected file
.It
Delete to remove selected file
.El

.Ss Read-Only Mode
With
.Fl r
or
.Cm set readonly
in command mode, all write operations are disabled.
Useful for safe inspection of remote systems.

.Sh COMMANDS
In command mode (press :), the following commands are available:
.Bl -tag -width "disconnect"
.It Cm connect Ar host
Connect to a different host.
.It Cm disconnect
Disconnect from current host.
.It Cm tab new
Create new tab.
.It Cm tab close
Close current tab.
.It Cm tab next, Cm tab prev
Switch tabs.
.It Cm split h, Cm split v
Split pane horizontally or vertically.
.It Cm fm toggle
Toggle file manager.
.It Cm fm refresh
Refresh file manager.
.It Cm set readonly, Cm set noreadonly
Toggle read-only mode.
.It Cm set theme Ar name
Change color theme.
.It Cm reload
Reload configuration.
.It Cm quit
Exit
.Nm .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/vis/config
Main configuration file.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/vis/vis.log
Log file (if enabled).
.It Pa ~/Downloads/vis/
Default local download directory.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width XDG_CONFIG_HOME
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
If set, configuration is read from
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vis/config
instead of
.Pa ~/.config/vis/config .
.It Ev HOME
Used to expand tilde in paths.
.It Ev TERM
Terminal type, overridden by configuration.
.It Ev SSH_AUTH_SOCK
Used for SSH agent authentication.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 on success, 1 on configuration or connection error,
2 on authentication failure, 3 on protocol error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Connect to the default university server:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ vis
.Ed
.Pp
Connect using a piped SSH command:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ ssh user@server.example.com | vis
.Ed
.Pp
Start in read-only mode:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ vis -r
.Ed
.Pp
Stop a running instance and clean history:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ vis -s -h
.Ed
.Pp
Use alternate config file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ vis -c ~/my-vis-config
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr sftp 1 ,
.Xr ssh_config 5 ,
.Xr SDL2 3 ,
.Xr libvterm 3
